  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have a television which had XXX working channels numbered 1,2,...,X1, 2, ..., X1,2,...,X. Unfortunately, due to a recent change, all **even**-numbered channels stopped working.\n\nFor example if X=5X = 5X=5, channels numbered 222 and 444 have stopped working, while channels numbered 111, 333 and 555 are still working.\n\nGiven XXX, can you tell how many channels are still working?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single integer XXX.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the number of working channels.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤1001 \\le X \\le 1001≤X≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAs explained in the statement, channels 111, 333 and 555 are still working, but channels 222 and 444 are not. Thus, the answer is 333."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100",
        "output": "50",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChannels 111, 333, 555, 777, ..., 999999 are still working. Carefully counting them, we know there are exactly 505050 working channels."
      }
    ]
  },
